# FROST, RFC 9591 section 5.3 (verify_signature_share): what a
# participant's two nonce commitments and key share commit to.  Three
# equations on one base, each with its own target, so each column is
# pinned by its own equation.
secrets d_i e_i sk_i
claims  d_i e_i sk_i
eq  hiding_commitment    G  1  1
eq  binding_commitment   1  G  1
eq  PK_i                 1  1  G

# An instance: one distinct generator per base name, so the
# environment is faithful and the verdict above transfers to it.
# The exponents are ours and carry no meaning; every element of a
# prime-order group is a generator power, so this is simply a way
# to write distinct elements down.
point G  2
